## 🛠️ How Security Researchers Find Gadgets (The Toolkit)
Because complex binaries contain millions of lines of machine instructions, researchers do not hunt for individual gadgets manually. They use specialized local automated command-line utilities to scan compiled binaries:

# Example: Using the 'ROPgadget' tool to automatically scan an executable file # This looks for snippets that let you control the 'rdi' register
ROPgadget --binary ./vulnerable_binary --only "pop|ret"

The tool returns exact hexadecimal memory locations mapping directly to found sequences like:
0x0000000000400683 : pop rdi ; ret
An attacker copies that exact location address into their Python struct.pack() exploit delivery payload script, chaining it alongside other functional blocks until they have built an automated blueprint that tricks the system into spawning a shell.
